WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.520
And so, let's all have a listen.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.270
Dear Hell...

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.570
Jigoku mitai ni asobitai
I want to have a good time like Hell

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.700
Jigoku mitai ni yasumitai
I want to rest like Hell

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.540
Jigoku mitai na nidoneshite
I want to go back to sleep like Hell

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.130
Teiji de agaritai
And finish work on time

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.970
Jigoku mitai ni tabesugite
I ate too much like Hell

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.720
Jigoku mitai ni nomisugita
I drank too much like Hell

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.980
Aa sonna wake de
Ah, for these reasons

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.230
Jigoku mitai
It's like Hell

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.650
Sonna toki koso deban desu
At such a time it's all the more his turn on stage

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.320
Hoozuki-sama ga moriageru
Mr. Hozuki livens things up

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.410
Omakase kudasai!
Please leave it to me!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:03.000
Aa jigoku jigoku mainichi jigoku
Ah, Hell, Hell, every day Hell

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.580
Jigoku jigoku
Hell, Hell

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.250
"Uso desho?!"
"You can't mean that, right?!"

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.170
Jigoku jigoku youkoso jigoku
Hell, Hell, welcome to Hell

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.010
Atchi muite
Look that way

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:14.590
Kotchi muite
Look this way

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.720
Abikyoukan!
Pandemonium!

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.090
Gongo! Doudan!
What the hell!

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.890
Shitsureishimashita!
Pardon me!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:23.890
Sonna kanji no
In that kind of way

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.980
A! Jigoku desu! Jajajajan!
Ah! It's Hell! Ta ta ta-da!

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.980
Katsu!
Curses!

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.320
THE LIVES OF MARQUIS DE SADE
AND LEOPOLD VON SACHER-MASOCH

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:44.410
And for that reason the etymology of "sadism"
is "Sade" and "masochism" comes from "Masoch."

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.290
The end.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.760
S-scary stuff!

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.220
Is that what they call a "standing ovation"?

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:16.820
Unrivaled at Poker

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.820
THE LIVES OF MARQUIS DE SADE
AND LEOPOLD VON SACHER-MASOCH

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.620
This book... Where did get it?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.450
Your bookshelf, Mr. Hozuki.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.170
I sense an indescribable madness...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.510
What's with this pervasive atmosphere that feels like
the inside of a mechanical-doll mansion?

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.840
Read one more.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.470
Next, this one.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.590
A Simple Beginner's Course
in Japanese Bondage Torture

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.720
I'm sorry, it's the end of my lunch break.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.390
I've received word from the Offices of Gokan that a
troublesome deceased will be arriving here momentarily,

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.270
so I need to get going.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.900
Their faces are so frightening... those three...

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.650
Well, they're simply sinister-looking
in general, you know?

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.410
They say that "men should be silent" and so on...

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.830
but in the case of Mr. Hozuki, it's more appropriate
to say he has a deadpan "Noh mask" face...

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.670
And when he gets angry it's like he has a
fierce-looking Noh mask plastered on his face...

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.790
And the Zashiki Warashi are Zashiki Warashi,

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:17.420
so it seems like sometime or other their heads
will turn 360 degrees or something...

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.880
Demons aren't scared of apparitions, are they?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.510
Eek!

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.560
Wh-wh-why are even you getting in
on the act, Mr. Hozuki?!

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:32.480
Well, with this talk of whether
I'm a Noh mask or a Tibet sand...

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.480
I didn't go as far as saying that!

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.440
The fact that he said that means someone
must've called him that before, right?

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:41.400
Wait, hold on. This is a good chance for me to say this...

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.990
Zashiki Warashi, you know...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.240
up till now I thought telling you this would
make you angry and you'd say it's discrimination, but...

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.160
It's best you learn to smile a little!

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.210
Being girls, that is!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.340
What about men?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.880
Let's just leave him out of this for now!

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.220
That's not what I mean!

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:09.100
Er, that's not what I'm talking about.
I mean that, on a gut level,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.690
I think girls are better when they're smiling!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:18.690
But, you know, aren't there some men
who decisively prefer girls who are mysterious like this?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:24.950
Certainly, there have long been some people
who've shown an attachment and fondness for that type.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.950
But, generally smiling cutely is to a girl's benefit
and it endears her with people, right?!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.080
Besides in the horror genre, are there any heroines
who have blank expressions throughout the story?!

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.750
Is that kinda thing actually cute?!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.710
Rei Ayan*mi

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.000
She's cute.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.670
Y-you're sure putting me on the spot...

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:46.970
That's its own thing! Besides, it's not like
she's completely expressionless, right?

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.390
When I look at these two, I get a bit worried.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.980
Well, it's not as if they're responsible
for attending to guests, but still...

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:57.150
Well, there is some truth in what you say.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.530
But, you know, when these twins laugh...

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:08.830
Ha
ha
ha
ha
Ha
ha
ha
ha

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:05.530
Ah, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha...

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.990
...it feels like the end times or something...
Ah, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha...

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:14.710
Note: A famous painting by Pablo Picasso.
I know this is rich coming from me,
but it's scary, kinda like Guernica or something?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.960
I know. And that's why we're going
to work to change that.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.420
First, a mirror! A mirror!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.510
Models and the like look at a mirror
and practice smiling and stuff, don't they?!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.220
My sis did that, too!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.640
That sister of mine...

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.640
Come on, now that's crazy!

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.480
I don't really get it, but like it! I do!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.690
Dang! This is funny stuff!

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.610
I like it! So good!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.070
What you looking at?! Not like I'm doin' anything wrong!

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.700
...is kind of like that. She's an example of a failure.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.830
Well, I think she's glorious and like her quite a bit...
And she's not two-faced in the slightest.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.710
Karauri, it's because of your plain fondness
for Miss O-Koh that you feel that way, isn't it?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.050
Ah... Well, Miss O-Koh certainly is elegant, after all.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.100
She's the ideal woman, as far as Karauri is concerned.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.890
You sure are annoying!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.520
There's nothing wrong
with having some class, you know!

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.100
Besides Miss O-Koh, Maki-Miki would also be fine,

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.650
but it's best to carefully select
who we use as a reference here!

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:28.360
Maki-Miki's pop-idol smiles
are something of a special skill, after all.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.780
Therein lies the rub.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.240
It's hopeless?

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.200
I wouldn't say it's "hopeless," but...

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:41.880
This complete lack of expression
is the Zashiki Warashi's forte,

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.380
so it's not something I'm particularly concerned about.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.630
Especially considering that we're in Hell.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.760
Mr. Hozuki!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.470
The deceased who has arrived
from the Offices of Gokan is complaining...

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:56.600
Oh, my apologies. I'll be right there.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.810
Er... more than just complaining,
he's being a total pain in the neck...

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.480
I sentence you to Inferno Hell!

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.200
And then...?

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.950
Inferno Hell means Inferno Hell!

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.240
You pretend to mean that, but...

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.290
He just goes on and on like that.
He's an extreme nuisance!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.210
Ah, so that's what you mean
by a deceased who's a "pain in the neck."

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.800
Even after the trial, he's still doing party tricks
and being all like,

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.800
"Alright, now I'll do an impersonation, so listen to this!"

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.640
We're having a hell of a time dealing with him.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:39.140
You should just hit him in the solar plexus
and haul him away after he shuts up.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.640
You're too lenient.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.740
Yeah.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.500
Alright.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.800
Well, then, please say something amusing.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.470
Quickly...

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.220
Looking forward to it...

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.970
Uh, let's see...

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:27.570
They totally crushed him in no time at all...
this trinity of Noh-masked-faced steel statues!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.950
If you can make these two laugh,
I may be open to reducing your sentence.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.030
I only promise that I'll consider it...

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:40.540
Huh?! Uh, well... This is pretty hard. What gives?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.670
Guys like him start to waver once they
actually become the center of attention...

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:52.130
By the way, if I laugh, it would simply provide me
some joy, so I'd be sure to give you something later.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.760
"Something"...

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.300
I'll give you a prune or the like.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.640
I don't need that!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.140
Uh, well, what do you want me to say here?

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:12.400
Alright, I'll say something, after which I ask that you
please respond with your usual "And then..."

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:18.070
After that I'll say something one more time,
and then you reply with a single word.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:22.370
Huh?! What? In the end do you close out
the performance or do I? Which is it?

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.620
This domination.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.210
And then...

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.210
Graduation.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.130
Yeah...

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:35.220
Huh?!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.260
DON'T GIVE ME A "YEAH"!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.850
YOU NEED TO RESPOND WITH SOMETHING FUNNY!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.310
See?!

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.600
TAKE A GOOD LOOK AT THE EYES OF THESE TWO!

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:54.320
I'm sorry! Please let me go on to the next trial!

00:09:55.150 --> 00:10:00.370
Please let me graduate beyond this demon
who asks the impossible!

