Hot Pick!
Straw Effigy Creation Workshop
Participants wanted!!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:03.870
They were helpful, right?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:09.540
When it comes to trials and Hell punishments,
being ominous is more likely to lead to favorable results.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:11.750
Hmm...

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.760
Well, I guess it's alright, then.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.130
If the twins themselves don't mind, that is...

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.220
They also take care of the goldfish plants, you know...

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.050
They're a big help to me.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.930
Well, I suppose it's fine, then. Sorry about that.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.560
Seems to have worked out well...
that you came to the Offices of Enma.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:10:59.880
Huh...?

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.430
Is Hell Your Intended Destination?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.430
Engineering
Department

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.640
You bastard!

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.230
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.900
What're you on abou-?!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.650
Your handwriting is too sloppy, you bastard!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.240
Say what?!

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.700
Isn't your job to create a clean copy of it?! Haggy Dome!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:30.870
Who you calling "Haggy Dome"?! Call me "Mr. Hagei"!
Can't believe how forgetful this guy is!

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.790
I agree with Mr. Hageito.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.250
Huh?! What did you say, Chief of Staff?!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:40.630
You guys are too detail-focused! You say my writing
is messy! That I write characters incorrectly!

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.760
Every other time you open your mouths,
it's "Use the correct meaning of words"

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.720
Use the correct
meaning of words

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:45.850
Use the correct
meaning of words
I see improper
potential verb forms

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.100
or "I see improper potential verb forms"!

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.640
It's so annoying!

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:53.520
Those are the kind of things...
a working member of society simply wouldn't mess up!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:53.850
Common sense
of working members
of society!!
Now's the time
to bring proper Japanese
to Hell!!
Records Department

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:58.280
You guys in the Records Department in particular
are always slicing hairs!

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:03.780
The phrase is "splitting hairs" or "picking nits," get it right!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.870
All you do is whine, whine, whine,
and point your finger at me!

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:07.740
What did you say?!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:12.540
If you have time to find fault, why don't you
try incorporating even one innovation?!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:17.630
How about YOU try keeping up
this minute work for a full year!

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.130
All in all, it's the substance that's important, right?!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.300
When it comes to words,
it's fine as long as the point gets across! That's all!

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:34.100
The substance isn't getting across, though.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.360
And that's why it's a problem.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.770
It's precisely as he says.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:43.950
Uzu, as a matter of fact, your handwriting is quite messy.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.780
Report
Regarding the manufacturing
case in which I was assassinated,
the screws need to
be made to order so ASAP...

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.570
Even you're supporting Haggy Dome now, Yomogi?!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:53.080
Fine, I get it. I'll fix my handwriting... But, you know...

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:59.880
"This here will be your coffee" is the kind of phrase
I often hear people use, but it sounds odd.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:04.050
Like I care! No way I can be bothered
with each instance of that stuff!

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:08.350
Well, yeah... If you go all the way back
to the mythological age,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.890
words really have changed a whole lot.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.680
There are different dialects now, too.

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:13.640
Right?!

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:18.650
Nowadays, we no longer use
"okashi" to mean "omobukifukai"...

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:15.520
Okashi (Strange)

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.900
Okashi (Strange)
Omobukifukai (Charming)

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.150
We don't even use "omobukifukai" at all!

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.070
That reminds me, women of that era often...

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.240
Okashi.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.200
Note: "Very charming."
Oh my, this is ito-okashi.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.160
...said things like that.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:39.250
The discussion got a bit off track, but the point is
that you make mistakes in an extreme way.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.000
This document's another example.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:48.800
Regarding the manufacturing case
in which I was assassinated,
the screws need to be made to order, so ASAP...

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.720
"Regarding the manufacturing case
in which I was assassinated,

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:48.090
the screws need to be made to order, so ASAP"...

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.640
Gah, can't read the rest.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:51.600
Uh-huh...

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.220
You get the nuance of it, right?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:57.190
I get that you meant to say "assigned," but...

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.440
Right, that's the one!

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:04.490
What's with your usage of "ASAP"?
And "assassinate" means "murder someone important."

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:07.860
Well, business terminology is overly difficult.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.990
There's no need to force yourself to use it, you know.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:15.500
By the way, I'm one of THOSE guys.
I hate the business term "win-win."

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:16.040
WIN
WIN

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:21.340
Generally, my counterpart will use it when it's
a 60 percent win for them and 40 percent win for me...

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.660
COUNTERPART

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:23.630
COUNTERPART
ME

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.670
all the while giving off an air of equality...

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.380
That air-quote gesture makes me so angry.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:30.800
Despite your haphazard phrasing,
you strike at the heart of the issue with these things...

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:35.350
Save those kind of comments
until you start using Japanese properly.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:40.270
Does the way you self-importantly preach like that
make you a damn little brat or damn old man?

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.560
You're a mix, making you a man-child.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.980
You sure don't hold back.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.860
It's 'cause guys like you ruin the atmosphere of a place!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:52.780
And punks like you are ruining the Japanese language!

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:56.500
Honestly, I'd say neither is free from blame.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.710
Hey now! Are you not gonna the same thing
to the demon Mon, who came from Thailand

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.540
and now works incredibly hard
at the local convenience store?!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:05.800
Ah, hallo!

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:10.090
That Mon fellow is a really good guy! Earlier, he said...

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.050
